.TH DANBY-MIGRATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-migration \- growth in two connected patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/migration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Temple/migration
is an interactive live simulation of growth in two connected patches.
It integrates the model continuously and redraws its state as parameters or
initial conditions change.
.SH MODEL
A'=rA(1-A)+m(B-A); B'=rB(1-B)-m(B-A).
.PP
A and B are patch populations, r local growth, and m migration strength.
.SH DISPLAY
Two time traces show local growth and equalizing migration. The heading reports current flow direction and magnitude.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the view to set both patch populations. Bottom tracks set growth and migration.
.PP
Space pauses or resumes the simulation.  Period advances one displayed step
while paused.  The
.B r
key restores the default initial state and
.B q
or Escape exits.
.SH INTERPRETATION
The quantities are normalized unless physical units are stated explicitly.
The display is a visualization of a low-dimensional differential-equation
model, not an agent simulation or a prediction of a particular real system.
Parameter changes restart the displayed history so trajectories from different
settings are not joined.
.SH NUMERICS
The state is advanced by the general-purpose
.B Numerics
fourth-order Runge-Kutta solver.  Small negative values caused by numerical
roundoff are clamped for nonnegative population and stock models.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/migration.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR numerics (2)

